LAST-MODIFIED:20260528T215026Z
UID:10000278-1782723600-1783087200@www.pollyklaastheater.org
SUMMARY:Dragons & Drama: Improv and D&D Camp
DESCRIPTION:We are delighted to be able to offer our summer camp experience for north bay kids again! \nOur camp\, taught by Carrie Caudle (RagTag Improv's artistic director and long-time Petaluma teacher) and Nickolas Rice (RagTag Improv player and children's theater veteran)\, is an engaging and inclusive experience for school-age children. Every day will involve a combination of interactive games\, fun acting exercises\, character development\, role-playing games\, crafts and other creative activities. \nNo improv or role-playing game experience is necessary; we'll teach it all! \nHere are some details: \nChildren ages 7-12 are welcome to enroll. \nCamp will be from Monday\, June 29th – Friday\, July 3rd. \nCamp hours: 9am-2pm Monday – Thursday & 9am-1pm Friday; Optional show for family and friends: 1:00 on Friday \nCamp location: Polly Klaas Community Theater\, Petaluma \nPlease send a snack\, lunch\, and water bottle with your child every day. \nCost: $400 \nTo complete enrollment\, please fill out this google form\, send payment (Venmo @carriecaudle or a check to RagTag Improv)\, and complete this online waiver: \nClick Here
URL:https://www.pollyklaastheater.org/event/dragons-drama-improv-and-dd-camp/
LOCATION:Polly Klaas Community Theater\, 417 Western Avenue\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.pollyklaastheater.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Drama-and-Dragons-Flyer.jpeg
END:VEVENT
